268
00:14:46,760 --> 00:14:49,560
You call me stupid, I'm stupid for football.

269
00:14:49,640 --> 00:14:52,940
This time I'll get past you! It's all about speed.

270
00:15:03,320 --> 00:15:07,790
He got past! He started with a slow dribble and suddenly increased his speed!

271
00:15:07,870 --> 00:15:11,290
This is a battle between an elegant bull and a flying wild hawk.

272
00:15:11,580 --> 00:15:14,040
This time, Tsubasa-kun won.

273
00:15:14,210 --> 00:15:15,380
Pierre.

274
00:15:15,460 --> 00:15:16,290
Tsubasa!

275
00:15:16,710 --> 00:15:20,510
Tsubasa-kun, even after passing Pierre-kun, increases his dribbling speed.

276
00:15:21,050 --> 00:15:22,970
I-Impossible.

277
00:15:23,090 --> 00:15:24,220
When it comes to France,

278
00:15:24,300 --> 00:15:27,810
Captain Pierre-kun was stunned by being passed by him.

279
00:15:28,350 --> 00:15:30,730
Roberto taught me this dribble.

280
00:15:31,390 --> 00:15:36,560
And Roberto may be flying to Brazil right now.

281
00:15:37,070 --> 00:15:39,230
This is from Roberto's notebook...

282
00:15:39,320 --> 00:15:40,570
This...

283
00:15:43,200 --> 00:15:44,570
Catch, here it comes!

284
00:15:44,860 --> 00:15:47,580
This is his special long-distance shot!

285
00:15:48,580 --> 00:15:51,830
Drive Shot!

286
00:15:52,960 --> 00:15:55,120
Splitting the rainy sky of France...

287
00:15:59,750 --> 00:16:03,720
Goal! Tsubasa-kun's Drive Shot!

288
00:16:05,130 --> 00:16:06,550
You did it, Tsubasa!

289
00:16:06,640 --> 00:16:07,970
We tied it up.

290
00:16:08,180 --> 00:16:09,140
They tied it up.

291
00:16:09,220 --> 00:16:10,560
In the 15th minute of the second half,

292
00:16:10,640 --> 00:16:14,730
the Japan team tied the score with 10 men.

293
00:16:15,140 --> 00:16:15,980
Great.

294
00:16:16,190 --> 00:16:17,270
We're tied.

295
00:16:17,360 --> 00:16:19,480
Your Drive Shot was great.

296
00:16:19,860 --> 00:16:21,320
Tsubasa-kun.

297
00:16:22,280 --> 00:16:24,150
Tsubasa, you were great.

298
00:16:24,400 --> 00:16:29,490
I taught you South America's long-distance Drive Shot perfectly.

299
00:16:29,990 --> 00:16:31,870
Just what you'd expect from Captain Tsubasa.

300
00:16:31,950 --> 00:16:34,790
Putting Misugi on the field was also the right decision, coach.

301
00:16:34,870 --> 00:16:35,710
Yes.

302
00:16:35,790 --> 00:16:38,880
Coach, I'm going to go tell Soda-san.

303
00:16:39,380 --> 00:16:42,420
The match started with a goal by Tsubasa-kun.

304
00:16:42,510 --> 00:16:46,800
However, France immediately responded with Pierre-kun's jumping shot.

305
00:16:46,880 --> 00:16:49,260
Then Soda-kun was sent off.

306
00:16:49,350 --> 00:16:52,140
And Pierre-kun comfortably made the score 2-1 with a penalty shot.

307
00:16:52,560 --> 00:16:55,480
Then France managed to score another goal with Napoleon-kun's shot.

308
00:16:55,560 --> 00:16:58,270
And they finished the first half 3-1 ahead.

309
00:16:59,650 --> 00:17:02,780
But in the second half, in the 7th minute,

310
00:17:03,110 --> 00:17:04,650
we saw Japan score with Hyuga-kun's shot.

311
00:17:04,940 --> 00:17:11,910
And now, in the 15th minute, Tsubasa-kun became the one to score and made the score 3-3.

312
00:17:12,200 --> 00:17:17,000
The equalizer that came after passing Pierre dealt a blow to the home team.

313
00:17:17,080 --> 00:17:17,920
Yes.

314
00:17:18,210 --> 00:17:21,090
The outcome of the game has become uncertain again.

315
00:17:21,250 --> 00:17:23,050
A-A tie?

316
00:17:23,130 --> 00:17:26,300
I see, the kids did it.

317
00:17:26,470 --> 00:17:29,550
15 minutes left and Japan has dominated the game.

318
00:17:29,640 --> 00:17:31,050
We can do it.

319
00:17:36,060 --> 00:17:39,060
I lost completely.

320
00:17:40,310 --> 00:17:42,150
Pi-Pierre.

321
00:17:42,230 --> 00:17:45,820
Long live France! Long live France!

322
00:17:45,900 --> 00:17:49,320
Long live France! Long live France!

323
00:17:49,410 --> 00:17:52,330
Long live France! Long live France!

324
00:17:52,740 --> 00:17:54,240
Be strong, France!

325
00:17:54,330 --> 00:17:56,830
It's still a tie and you haven't lost!

326
00:17:57,080 --> 00:17:59,710
If you play your own football, you'll win!

327
00:17:59,790 --> 00:18:02,340
Be strong, France!

328
00:18:02,670 --> 00:18:07,550
That's right, we have a bunch of passionate fans.

329
00:18:08,260 --> 00:18:12,220
We cannot embarrass ourselves in front of our fans!

330
00:18:13,970 --> 00:18:15,640
They are short players.

331
00:18:15,720 --> 00:18:19,060
As the game progresses, they will get tired.

332
00:18:19,140 --> 00:18:22,150
We may have equalized, but we are still at an advantage.

333
00:18:22,230 --> 00:18:23,610
Don't give up.

334
00:18:24,150 --> 00:18:24,980
Okay.

335
00:18:27,150 --> 00:18:28,950
Alright, we're attacking, guys.

336
00:18:30,030 --> 00:18:32,910
France gained morale from the cheers of the fans.

337
00:18:32,990 --> 00:18:34,490
And they attack fearlessly.

338
00:18:34,830 --> 00:18:36,370
We must defend solidly until the end.

339
00:18:36,450 --> 00:18:37,250
Okay.

340
00:18:39,750 --> 00:18:41,120
Defend!

341
00:18:41,370 --> 00:18:43,630
Attack! Score a goal!

342
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:48,630
But Japan defends more solidly with Misugi-kun.

343
00:18:49,010 --> 00:18:51,380
They no longer concede goals easily.

344
00:18:51,970 --> 00:18:54,180
They also have an offside specialist.

345
00:18:54,260 --> 00:18:56,890
We can't send the ball in front of the goal without thinking.

346
00:18:59,430 --> 00:19:00,770
Catch, Napoleon!

347
00:19:02,190 --> 00:19:03,020
What?

348
00:19:03,310 --> 00:19:05,520
This was an unexpected return pass.

349
00:19:05,690 --> 00:19:07,530
Good, now I'll score.

350
00:19:07,940 --> 00:19:11,240
This is France's forward, Louis Napoleon...

351
00:19:13,490 --> 00:19:16,160
Cannon Shot!

352
00:19:24,540 --> 00:19:30,420
But Napoleon-kun's long-distance shot was stopped by goalkeeper Wakashimazu.

353
00:19:30,590 --> 00:19:31,420
Damn it.

354
00:19:31,590 --> 00:19:33,180
You were great, Wakashimazu.

355
00:19:34,720 --> 00:19:38,180
The damage Schneider caused me at the beginning of the tournament...

356
00:19:38,260 --> 00:19:40,430
caused my right hand to weaken a bit.

357
00:19:41,180 --> 00:19:42,690
That goalkeeper...

358
00:19:43,230 --> 00:19:46,900
In the first International Youth Tournament in France,

359
00:19:46,980 --> 00:19:50,190
the two teams defend and attack like table tennis.

360
00:19:50,440 --> 00:19:51,570
Go to the goal!

361
00:19:51,740 --> 00:19:52,820
Cut them off!

362
00:19:52,950 --> 00:19:54,660
Don't let them hold the ball!

363
00:19:56,910 --> 00:19:59,580
Because of the rain that started in the second half,

364
00:19:59,910 --> 00:20:02,580
the ground has become very wet and muddy.

365
00:20:02,870 --> 00:20:06,460
The seconds flow by, unaffected by the air.

366
00:20:07,210 --> 00:20:09,590
Less than 10 minutes left.

367
00:20:09,960 --> 00:20:15,340
Whoever scores the next goal will win the match.

368
00:20:20,220 --> 00:20:22,850
Tsubasa-kun controls the ball.

369
00:20:23,140 --> 00:20:26,230
Again number 10, don't leave him alone!

370
00:20:26,310 --> 00:20:27,860
Mark him, France!

371
00:20:28,020 --> 00:20:29,860
- Damn it.
- Crush him!

372
00:20:30,150 --> 00:20:31,980
France tackles!

373
00:20:32,190 --> 00:20:33,240
Nice.

374
00:20:33,490 --> 00:20:37,240
But Tsubasa-kun jumps and passes in the air.

375
00:20:37,910 --> 00:20:39,240
The ball goes to Misaki-kun.

376
00:20:39,530 --> 00:20:42,250
But Pierre-kun stands in Misaki-kun's path.

377
00:20:42,330 --> 00:20:46,500
Like Tsubasa-kun, will Misaki-kun challenge him one-on-one?

378
00:20:48,250 --> 00:20:49,790
No, he passes.

379
00:20:49,880 --> 00:20:51,250
Come on, Misaki-kun.

380
00:20:51,500 --> 00:20:54,260
This is a wonderful one-two with Tsubasa-kun.

381
00:20:55,340 --> 00:20:57,760
Just as I thought, now I'll intercept that pass.

382
00:20:58,010 --> 00:21:01,760
But will Pierre-kun understand and intercept the pass?

383
00:21:03,930 --> 00:21:04,770
What!?

384
00:21:05,230 --> 00:21:08,520
Pierre-kun slips on the muddy ground!

385
00:21:10,610 --> 00:21:12,070
I'll cut him off.

386
00:21:12,320 --> 00:21:13,150
Nice.

387
00:21:13,400 --> 00:21:14,240
Kojiro.

388
00:21:14,320 --> 00:21:17,160
Misaki-kun gives the final pass to Hyuga-kun.

389
00:21:17,320 --> 00:21:19,160
- Damn it.
- No!

390
00:21:19,240 --> 00:21:22,830
A wonderful pass through the French defense.

391
00:21:22,910 --> 00:21:24,160
Good, I caught it.

392
00:21:24,250 --> 00:21:27,580
I, Kojiro Hyuga, will score the winning goal.

393
00:21:30,210 --> 00:21:31,040
What?

394
00:21:31,130 --> 00:21:32,880
Oh, he stopped!

395
00:21:32,960 --> 00:21:35,920
Hyuga-kun can't shoot like this!

396
00:21:37,010 --> 00:21:38,010
We're saved.

397
00:21:38,090 --> 00:21:41,720
This puddle was truly a chance for France.

398
00:21:41,800 --> 00:21:42,810
Now the loose ball,

399
00:21:42,890 --> 00:21:46,100
is picked up by the returning forward Napoleon-kun.

400
00:21:46,730 --> 00:21:49,940
As if the goddess of victory is smiling upon us.

401
00:21:50,310 --> 00:21:51,560
Let's advance, Pierre.

402
00:21:51,650 --> 00:21:52,820
Napoleon.

403
00:21:53,480 --> 00:21:55,610
Good luck, France!

404
00:21:55,690 --> 00:21:59,200
Time to make the ultimate attack!

405
00:21:59,450 --> 00:22:03,490
Let's go! France's Eiffel Tower Attack!

406
00:22:03,580 --> 00:22:05,620
Eiffel Tower Attack?

407
00:23:46,670 --> 00:23:50,030
Next Episode: Misaki vs Pierre